# M10 — User management: status

Updated: 2026-11-21 · App: Mieruka · Team: Zero-Ichi

## Decisions

- M10 is the user management module: accounts, roles and login with Google.
- 2026-11-21: Google login is built with django-allauth inside the Django app (chosen over Clerk and a separate FastAPI service: fewest moving parts on Vercel).
- Staff access to the M5 back office is granted to Google accounts whose verified email is listed in `MIERUKA_STAFF_EMAILS`.
- There is no email/password sign-up. Django staff passwords (`createsuperuser`) still work through "Staff password login".

## Current state

- Created with `uv run manage.py startapp m10`, registered in `config/settings.py` and routed at `/m10/`.
- `/m10/` is the sign-in page: "Continue with Google", account status, link to the back office, sign out.
- Google OAuth via `allauth.socialaccount.providers.google`, routes under `/accounts/` (callback `/accounts/google/login/callback/`).
- `m10/adapters.py`: closes local sign-up, opens Google sign-up, makes listed emails staff (never removes staff rights).
- Settings read `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID`, `GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET` and `MIERUKA_STAFF_EMAILS` from the environment; without the Google keys the page says sign-in is not configured.
- On Vercel, Django trusts the HTTPS proxy header so the callback URL uses https.
- Not yet: linking a Google account to its household (`Utilisateur.compte`), household role for M4.
- Tests: `m10/tests.py` (sign-in page, safe `next`, staff rule, closed sign-up, https callback).

